// Vector.copy() is a conditional method: it only exists when the element type
// can be duplicated (`extension Vector<T: ExplicitCopy>` — design 219, since the
// body spells `buf[i].copy()`). `Vector<File>` has a move-only element that
// cannot be duplicated at all, so copy() does not exist for it and the call is a
// compile-time error naming the unmet bound. (Diagnostic improved from the old
// codegen-time "cannot copy value of type `File`" to this typechecker-time
// bound diagnostic.)
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: type `Vector<File, GlobalAllocator>` has no method `copy`
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: requires `T: ExplicitCopy`, and `File` does not conform

func main() {
    var v = Vector<File>()
    let w = v.copy()
    print(w.len())
}
